    },
    {
      "id": "bcb010f6d92e1186a6654dfeddbde008338ad947",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 958017367,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Unsigned numbers also exist to allocate amounts of memory to fit a table, which is what is happening here, and the conceptual nature of the integer as non-negative is relevant.\n\nIf there is overflow or the number take a negative value, then there's a logic problem in the code. gcc is giving the error since on LP64 platforms `int` is 32 bit but `gsize` (which `g_malloc` takes) is an `unsigned long`, meaning that if it *does* take -1, it's wrapping around in a way that we don't expect. (In practice this doesn't happen, but the compiler doesn't know that.)\n\nIt is possible to avoid the warning by casting `borderlen` from `int` to `unsigned int` only at the `g_malloc` line, though.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2022-05-24T11:35:16.335Z",
          "updated_at": "2022-05-24T11:35:16.335Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 156765693,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 7003,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "610cb27e45e4839532099ef523e2cc38533ed96e",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 958045742,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Well, obviously. Saying the code _could_ have logical errors is not much of a warning either. I knew that already. I don't need to be reminded.\n\nAnyway I'm not opposed to merging this to squelch this bugger.",
